            <ArticleTitle>A rare complication of coronary arteriography.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>455-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a 66-year-old man with acute mesenteric ischemia and myocardial ischemia within 6 hr after coronary arteriography. He underwent successful emergency surgery with embolectomy of the mesenteric artery and coronary artery bypass grafting.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
